    "https://schreiner.edu/job/security-officer-ii/": {
      "title": "Schreiner University",
      "description": "Security Officer II - Schreiner University Skip to content Request Information Anonymous Reporting Toggle Navigation Library Calendar Map Visit Canvas Schreiner One IT Support Academy Prep Shop Toggle Navigation Admissions Academics Campus Life Athletics About Giving Alumni News Search Apply Now Toggle Navigation Admissions Academic Campus Life Athletics About Giving Alumni Visit Us Apply Now Shop Schreiner Quick Links News Library Event Calendar Campus Map Schreiner One Canvas Security Officer II Full Time Kerrville Texas Posted 1 week ago Website schreineru Schreiner University Security Officer II SUMMARY OF RESPONSIBILITIES The Security Officer II is responsible for protecting individuals on campus property and maintaining the security of campus buildings, facilities, parking lots, walkways, and grounds of the University. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Act as first responder to all campus emergencies, medical and criminal, that could potentially be hazardous and/or life threatening. Enforce campus policies and procedures as may relate to safety and security concerns. Assist Residence and Student Life with enforcement of hall regulations and Code of Conduct Violations. Make regular inspection tours of the campus facilities noting unusual occurrences. Watch for trespassers, fire, water leaks, or other circumstances which could lead to loss or damage to property and equipment. Unlock buildings as scheduled for events and ensures all windows and doors are locked as scheduled. Observe and report hazardous conditions to management. Ensure inside and outside lights are turned on/off as required and informs supervisor when any electrical or mechanical system is malfunctioning. Ensure only authorized persons are admitted to the campus while on duty. Direct visitors and assists, as necessary. Monitor parking lots and direct traffic and parking, as necessary. Enforce campus traffic regulations including parking, and speeding. Enforce campus policies including tobacco usage, alcohol usage, and drug usage. Observe weather conditions on campus and report dangerous or unusual weather-related activity to management. Complete investigations of University violations, including viewing camera footage, talking with witnesses, and writing incident reports. Act as a liaison for the University with local law enforcement. Provide awareness education/information on an informal basis to students and employees during other duties. Performs other duties as assigned. EDUCATION, EXPERIENCE AND SKILLS REQUIRED High school diploma or GED Ability to obtain a Security Guard License issued by the State of Texas. Successfully pass the Non-commissioned and Commissioned exams of the Texas Board of Private Investigators and Securities Act (Provided by the University). Ability to become a Clery Act reporting official upon completing of training. Previous work experience in a University public safety/security department preferred. 1 to 3 years’ experience preferred in a public/campus safety position. Must have a valid Texas driver’s license, related insurance and good driving record. WORKING CONDITIONS: Work environment involves some exposure to hazards or physical risks, which require following basic safety precautions. Work may involve moderate exposure to unusual elements, such as extreme temperatures, dirt, dust, fumes, smoke, unpleasant odors, and/or loud noises. Moderate physical activity; requires handling of average-weight objects and standing or walking for extended periods of time. Apply for Job Schreiner University 2100 Memorial Blvd Kerrville, TX 78028 Directions | 830.896.5411 Financial Services | 830.792.7303 FinancialServices@schreiner.edu Admissions | 830.792.7217 admissions@schreiner.edu Office Hours: 8am – 5pm, Mon -Fri Prospective Students Request Information Apply Financial Services Transcript Requests FAQ Consumer Information Directory About Visitors Donor Alumni Careers at Schreiner Graduate Assistantship Campus Map Schreiner Experiences Box Office Library & Textbooks Schreiner Technology Schreiner Retail Store Community Supporters SU2030 Strategic Plan Security Title IX Privacy Policy CARES Act and HEERF © Schreiner University | 2100 Memorial Blvd. Kerrville, TX 78028-5611 – 830.896.5411 Financial Services: 830.792.7303 – FinancialServices@schreiner.edu Admissions: 830.792.7217 – admissions@schreiner.edu ANONYMOUS REPORTING Campus Conduct Hotline: 866-943-5787 Page load link Search Schreiner Resources Academic Programs Financial Services University Directory Students | Faculty | Staff Schreiner One Canvas Pounce This site uses cookies and other third-party services. For more information please see our Privacy Policy . Accept & Close Go to Top"
